Codex suits developers and teams who already pay for ChatGPT and want one agent across the terminal, the editor and the cloud, and teams that want AI review on every pull request. Developers who prefer Anthropic's models or want to switch between vendors should also look at Claude Code, Cursor or GitHub Copilot.$t$, ARRAY[$t$Included in ChatGPT plans, so Plus, Pro and Business subscribers get Codex without a separate subscription$t$, $t$One agent across the ChatGPT apps, CLI, IDE extension and Codex cloud, tied to one ChatGPT account$t$, $t$Runs agents in parallel and keeps cloud tasks going after you close your laptop$t$, $t$Automatic pull request review plus GitHub, GitLab (beta), Slack and Linear integrations$t$, $t$Open-source Codex CLI (Apache-2.0) for macOS, Linux and Windows$t$]::text[], ARRAY[$t$Plus and Business usage is capped per five-hour window, and GPT-6.1 Sol uses the allowance fastest$t$, $t$Free and Go plans only get the lightweight GPT-6 Luna model in the desktop app$t$, $t$Heavy daily use pushes you toward Pro at $100 to $500 a month or extra credits$t$, $t$Works only with OpenAI models, unlike multi-vendor tools such as Cursor or GitHub Copilot$t$, $t$Agent changes and shell access still need careful review and permission settings$t$]::text[], $t$["✅ You already pay for ChatGPT Plus, Pro or Business and want a coding agent included", "✅ You want to hand off whole tasks, such as bug fixes, refactors and tests, and review the result", "✅ You want automatic AI review on every pull request", "✅ You move between terminal, editor and cloud and want the same agent everywhere"]$t$::jsonb, $t$[{"q": "What is OpenAI Codex?", "a": "OpenAI Codex is OpenAI's coding agent. It takes tasks such as fixing bugs, refactoring, adding features and writing tests, works through your repository and returns changes for review. It runs in the ChatGPT apps, the Codex CLI, an IDE extension and Codex cloud, and can also review pull requests automatically."}, {"q": "Is OpenAI Codex free?", "a": "Partly. The ChatGPT Free plan and Go ($8 a month) include lightweight Codex use in the desktop app with the GPT-6 Luna model, subject to rollout. Full Codex on the web, CLI, IDE extension and iOS starts with ChatGPT Plus at $20 a month. Pro costs $100, $200 or $500 a month, and Business is $20 per user per month billed annually or $25 billed monthly."}, {"q": "Which models does Codex use?", "a": "As of October 2026, OpenAI lists GPT-6.1 Sol, GPT-6 Sol, GPT-6 Luna and GPT-6 Astra for Codex. Plus users get GPT-6.1 Sol and GPT-6 Luna. GPT-5.5 was retired from Codex for ChatGPT sign-in on October 14, 2026."}, {"q": "What are the Codex usage limits?", "a": "On Plus and Business, Codex usage is measured per five-hour window. OpenAI estimates about 15 to 160 local messages per five hours with GPT-6.1 Sol and 350 to 3,000 with GPT-6 Luna. Pro currently has no five-hour limit, and Plus, Pro and Business users can buy extra credits."}]$t$::jsonb, NULL, ARRAY[$t$claude-code$t$, $t$cursor$t$, $t$github-copilot$t$]::text[], false, $t$2026-10-25$t$::date)
