Granola suits founders, managers, investors and sales or customer teams who sit in many meetings, dislike meeting bots and want to keep taking their own notes with AI filling in the gaps. Teams that want a bot-based recorder with video replay may prefer Otter.ai or Fireflies.ai.$t$, ARRAY[$t$No bot joins the call: captures audio from your device across Zoom, Meet, Teams, huddles and in-person meetings$t$, $t$Builds on your own rough notes instead of replacing them with a generic summary$t$, $t$Apps for Mac, Windows, iPhone, Android and Apple Watch$t$, $t$MCP connector and API bring meeting notes into Claude, ChatGPT and Cursor$t$, $t$Supports 32 languages since September 2026$t$]::text[], ARRAY[$t$Free Basic plan only shows the last 30 days of meeting history$t$, $t$Pre-meeting briefs, follow-up emails, integrations and API need the $14 Business plan$t$, $t$SSO, SCIM and admin controls only on the $35 Enterprise plan$t$, $t$With no bot, other participants are not automatically told they are being transcribed; the org-wide notice is still a pilot$t$]::text[], $t$["✅ You dislike meeting bots and want notes captured quietly from your own device", "✅ You like to take your own notes and want AI to fill in the gaps", "✅ You want your meeting history available in Claude, ChatGPT or Cursor through MCP", "✅ Your team wants shared folders and chat across everyone's meetings"]$t$::jsonb, $t$[{"q": "What is Granola?", "a": "Granola is an AI notepad for meetings. It transcribes audio from your computer or phone without a bot joining the call and turns your rough notes plus the transcript into structured notes, action items and follow-ups. It works with Zoom, Google Meet, Teams, Slack huddles and in-person meetings."}, {"q": "Is Granola free?", "a": "Yes, the Basic plan is free and includes AI meeting notes, chat, shared folders and templates, but you can only see the last 30 days of meeting history. Business costs $14 per user per month for unlimited history, briefs, follow-up emails, integrations, MCP and API access. Enterprise costs $35 per user per month."}, {"q": "Does Granola use a meeting bot?", "a": "No. Granola records audio from your own device, so no bot appears in the call. That also means other participants are not automatically notified, so you should tell them you are taking AI notes. An organization-wide notification is available as a pilot on Enterprise."}, {"q": "Which platforms does Granola support?", "a": "Granola has apps for macOS, Windows, iOS and Android, plus an Apple Watch app launched in July 2026. It also connects to AI tools such as Claude, ChatGPT and Cursor through its MCP connector."}]$t$::jsonb, NULL, ARRAY[$t$otter-ai$t$, $t$fireflies-ai$t$, $t$notion-ai$t$]::text[], false, $t$2026-10-25$t$::date)
ON CONFLICT (slug, lang) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO tools (slug, lang, name, url, domain, category, badge, users, best_for, description, description_long, pros, cons, choose_if, faq, rating, also_consider, published, last_updated) VALUES ($t$photoroom$t$, $t$en$t$, $t$Photoroom$t$, $t$https://www.photoroom.com$t$, $t$photoroom.com$t$, $t$design$t$, $t$freemium$t$, $t$80M+$t$, $t$E-commerce product photos: background removal, AI backgrounds and models, batch editing, API$t$, $t$Photoroom is an AI photo editor for product photography that removes backgrounds, adds shadows and AI-generated scenes, and batch-edits catalog images on mobile, web and through an API. The company says it is trusted by more than 80 million users and 1 million businesses.$t$, $t$Photoroom is an AI photo editor built for people who sell online, from marketplace sellers and small shops to large retailers. It started as a background remover and now covers the whole product-image workflow: cutting out the product, adding shadows, staging it in AI-generated scenes, putting clothing on AI fashion models and producing short product videos for ads.

As of October 2026, Photoroom offers a Free plan and four paid plans: Pro, Max, Ultra and Enterprise. Paid plans combine unlimited core tools (within fair use) with a monthly pool of AI credits for heavier generation features. On its website the company says it is trusted by 80M+ users and 1M+ businesses.

Core tools include the Background Remover, Retouch, AI Product Fixer, preset AI Shadows, AI Fill, AI Expand and Resize, Image Enhancer and Recolor. Credit-based tools include AI Backgrounds Studio, AI Fashion Models, AI Images, Edit with AI, adjustable AI shadows and the Video Generator. Batch editing handles thousands of images in one job, Spaces let teams of up to 50 seats share designs and a Brand Kit, Max and Ultra connect to Shopify, and a REST API and MCP server bring Photoroom into your own systems and AI assistants. The apps run on iOS, Android and the web.

US prices: Pro costs $12.99 a month billed monthly or $89.99 a year, with 8,000 AI credits and 1,000 exports a month. Max costs $34.99 a month or $249.99 a year, with 25,000 credits, 3,000 exports, the Video Generator and Shopify integration. Ultra costs $99 a month or $990 a year, with 75,000 credits, 10,000 exports and 4K image and video output. Enterprise is a custom annual contract with one shared balance across the apps and API. Pro and Max yearly plans include a 7-day free trial, each paid plan includes an API and MCP credit wallet worth the plan's price, and prices and credit amounts vary by country.

The Free plan has limited features, lower credit and export limits, no API access and is for personal, non-commercial use only. Exports on paid plans are capped each month and pause when you hit the limit. Credit-heavy features run out fast: Max allows up to about 50 video generations a month, and 4K output is only on Ultra.

Photoroom suits online sellers, e-commerce teams and marketplaces that need consistent, high-volume product photos and listing images. For general graphic design and social layouts, Canva is broader; for full creative control, Adobe Firefly and Photoshop go further.$t$, ARRAY[$t$Fast, accurate background removal plus shadows, retouching and AI product fixes on every paid plan$t$, $t$AI backgrounds, fashion models and product videos built specifically for listings and ads$t$, $t$Batch editing for thousands of images and a Shopify integration on Max and Ultra$t$, $t$Available on iOS, Android and web, with a REST API and MCP server$t$, $t$Paid plans include an API credit wallet worth the plan price$t$]::text[], ARRAY[$t$Free plan is for personal, non-commercial use only and has no API access$t$, $t$Monthly export caps pause downloads until the next billing cycle$t$, $t$Video and high-resolution generation use credits quickly; 4K is only on Ultra at $99 a month$t$, $t$Prices and monthly credit allowances vary by country$t$]::text[], $t$["✅ You sell online and need clean product photos with white or AI-generated backgrounds", "✅ You edit large catalogs and want batch processing or a Shopify connection", "✅ You want clothing shown on AI models without a photo shoot", "✅ You want to automate product images through an API or an AI assistant"]$t$::jsonb, $t$[{"q": "What is Photoroom used for?", "a": "Photoroom is used to create product photos for online stores and marketplaces. It removes backgrounds, adds shadows, places products in AI-generated scenes, puts clothing on AI fashion models, makes short product videos and batch-edits whole catalogs."}, {"q": "Is Photoroom free?", "a": "There is a Free plan with limited features and lower credit and export limits, for personal, non-commercial use only and without API access. In the US, Pro costs $12.99 a month or $89.99 a year, Max $34.99 a month or $249.99 a year, and Ultra $99 a month or $990 a year. Pro and Max yearly plans include a 7-day free trial."}, {"q": "What are Photoroom AI credits?", "a": "AI credits pay for the heavier tools, such as the Video Generator, AI Fashion Models, AI Backgrounds Studio and Edit with AI. Pro includes 8,000 credits a month, Max 25,000 and Ultra 75,000. Core tools like the Background Remover and Retouch do not use credits on paid plans."}, {"q": "Does Photoroom have an API?", "a": "Yes. Photoroom offers a REST API and an MCP server for tools like Claude. Each paid plan includes a wallet of API and MCP credits worth the plan's price, and API usage does not count against your export allowance. The Free plan has no API access."}]$t$::jsonb, NULL, ARRAY[$t$canva-ai$t$, $t$adobe-firefly$t$, $t$adcreative-ai$t$]::text[], false, $t$2026-10-25$t$::date)
ON CONFLICT (slug, lang) DO NOTHING;
